cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it together with the EVOLVEpro method it reimplements."
title: plm-evolve
abstract: >-
  Independent implementation of the EVOLVEpro core principle: frozen protein
  language model embeddings feeding a top-layer RandomForest active-learning
  loop for experimental directed evolution, with a research layer of
  acquisition, batch-diversity, multi-mutant, and multi-objective capabilities.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "the plm-evolve contributors"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - protein
  - directed-evolution
  - protein-language-model
  - active-learning
  - esm2
  - esmc
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Rapid in silico directed evolution by a protein language model with EVOLVEpro"
    authors:
      - family-names: Jiang
        given-names: Kaiyi
    year: 2025
    journal: Science
    doi: 10.1126/science.adr6006
  - type: article
    title: "Evolutionary-scale prediction of atomic-level protein structure with a language model"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lin
        given-names: Zeming
    year: 2023
    journal: Science
    doi: 10.1126/science.ade2574
  - type: software
    title: "ESM-C (ESM Cambrian)"
    authors:
      - name: "EvolutionaryScale"
    year: 2024
    notes: "Frozen PLM backend (esmc_300m / esmc_600m), accessed via the esm SDK."
